docs/decisions.md:179:The owner answered every row of the 2026-11-05 decision page, in the terminal. The rows that revise a recorded rule were answered one by one: Q5.1/Q5.4, Q6.4, Q2.8, Q9.15 with P3, Q7.11 and Q4.7. Q3.12, Q9.19, Q7.10, Q1.6, P2, P4, P9, P13, P16 and P17a/b were also answered directly. The remaining Core rows were accepted as recommended, and the remaining project rows were approved on the owner's condition that Claude and Codex agree and that each is the best long-term design (both confirmed; every row carries Codex agreement). The full rows (question, options, reason, recommendation, agreement, revision and notes) are in [core_rows.json](archive/decisions-2026-11-05/core_rows.json) and [other_rows.json](archive/decisions-2026-11-05/other_rows.json); the concrete rules behind them are in [R4_RATIONALE.md](archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md), and where R4 and a row differ, the row governs.
docs/decisions.md:181:**The Core rows are a provisional approval (stage A2a).** They bind the design without freezing it. Stage A2b formalizes them in a proposed `ConcreteSpec/Spec.lean` and proves the four design theorems; any row the formalization changes returns to the owner; stage A2i integrates the parts (2026-11-06); the owner freezes Core at A2c (row Q9.19 as revised). Until a rule is written in Lean, the answer below governs over any chapter text that differs.
docs/decisions.md:188:- **The generated-chapter requirement** (rows Q9.15, P3): Lean is the specification, in one main normative file with doc comments and examples; no prose is generated from it. This confirms the [2026-11-04 decision](#decided-project-lean-is-the-spec). The "one main normative file" wording is revised 2026-11-06 by the [long-term changes](#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06): one authoritative specification library in cohesive modules, with `ConcreteSpec/Spec.lean` as its public import.
docs/decisions.md:192:- <a id="decided-2026-11-05-q9-1-reads"></a>**Q9.1, read forms** (owner-confirmed, 2026-11-05): `copy x` is allowed only when `x` has a Copy type and `move x` only when it has a non-Copy (linear) type. Each read has one form; `move` of a Copy value and `copy` of a linear value are both refused.
docs/decisions.md:237:- **Q4.7** How are scoped views and range subviews introduced? — (a) borrow [mut] source [from a until b] as view { … } [else { … }]; no else = trap (like indexing); proven invalid range without else refused (OD118). *Revises or adds: Replaces R4 F4.3 text-only mandatory-else form; extends Q3.1/Q3.2 with subview formation; preserves OD36/OD118.* *Revised 2026-11-06 by [no hidden traps](#decided-project-no-hidden-traps): the form without `else` needs evidence of a valid range; a provably out-of-range view index is covered by the same rule.* *Revised 2026-11-08 by the [language decisions](#decided-2026-11-08-language-revisions): the form is `borrow [mut] view = source [from a until b] { ... } [else { ... }]`.*
docs/decisions.md:267:- **Q9.1** What is Core’s expression and binding form? — ANF; fresh identities; explicit moves/copies; separate places. *Confirmed 2026-11-05: `copy` only for Copy types, `move` only for non-Copy types ([read forms](#decided-2026-11-05-q9-1-reads)).*
docs/decisions.md:268:- **Q9.2** What types and declaration identities must Core represent? — Kinded nominal inventory; ordinary owning container definitions.
docs/decisions.md:269:- **Q9.3** What is the single loop form? — Core `while L { C } do { B }`: C is a condition region re-run every iteration; the counted loop advances its counter before the body.
docs/decisions.md:270:- **Q9.4** How are data, matching and exits represented? — Flat data/matches; structured exits; checked stores.
docs/decisions.md:271:- **Q9.5** Are heap opening and borrowing separate user mechanisms? — One surface borrow; distinct typed Core cases. *Revised 2026-11-08 by the [language decisions](#decided-2026-11-08-language-revisions): the one surface borrow is written `borrow [mut] view = source ...`.*
docs/decisions.md:272:- **Q9.6** Which operations are primitives rather than ordinary definitions? — Irreducible primitives; checked destructor bodies.
docs/decisions.md:273:- **Q9.7** How are primitive calls specified? — One exhaustive typed primitive-contract inventory. *Revised 2026-11-08 by the [foundation decision](#foundation-q16): lawful registry instances rather than a permanently closed inventory; exhaustive coverage of the selected registry; an unknown operation is refused.*
docs/decisions.md:274:- **Q9.8** Does `defer` survive in Core? — Nested deferred scopes; late reads; reverse cleanup.
docs/decisions.md:275:- **Q9.9** What is evaluator state and execution style? — Total clock-indexed evaluator; explicit instrumented state.
docs/decisions.md:276:- **Q9.10** How are ownership instrumentation and erasure organized? — Ghost ownership instrumentation with proved erasure.
docs/decisions.md:277:- **Q9.11** What do contracts mean and when are they checked? — Erased logical contracts; ensures sees result and surviving parameters after cleanup; no snapshot construct. *Revised 2026-11-06 by [no hidden traps](#decided-project-no-hidden-traps): a claim used for safety admission needs closed evidence.*
docs/decisions.md:278:- **Q9.12** What evidence crosses declaration/module interfaces? — Checked semantic interfaces with reviewable declarations.
docs/decisions.md:279:- **Q9.13** Are judgments independent of the checker and elaborator? — Independent judgments; checker/elaborator correspondence.
docs/decisions.md:280:- **Q9.14** What must pass before Core freezes? — Provisional approval, then four kernel-checked theorems against a proposed Spec.lean, then freeze. Revised 2026-11-06 by the [long-term changes](#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06): the integration stage A2i (interaction proofs, semantic contract, modular layout, owner view, outside-reader pass) also passes before the freeze.
docs/decisions.md:281:- **Q9.15** Where do normative definitions and documentation live? — One main normative Lean file with doc comments. *Revises or adds: Generated-chapter requirement (philosophy rule 6 / earlier roadmap commitment): replaced by one normative Lean file with doc comments and examples, a browsable rendering of that Lean, and coverage-gated retirement of prose chapters; your decision of 2026-11-04.*
docs/decisions.md:282:- **Q9.16** What Lean dependencies may the specification use? — Core Lean; supporting Batteries; owner exceptions for Mathlib.
docs/decisions.md:283:- **Q9.17** May spec proofs use `native_decide`? — Kernel-only authoritative spec/A2 proofs.
docs/decisions.md:284:- **Q9.18** How is the old compiler retained? — Frozen isolated `legacy/`; no normative fallback.
docs/decisions.md:285:- **Q9.19** How do approval, formalization and Core freeze relate? — A2a → A2b → A2c; Spec.lean headed PROPOSED until freeze; R-0560 depends on the freeze. *Revises or adds: Process: owner decision.* Revised 2026-11-06 by the [long-term changes](#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06): integration (A2i) comes between A2b and the A2c freeze, and the modular layout (R-0560) precedes the freeze.
docs/decisions.md:291:- **P3** Lean is the spec: confirm the amendment — Lean is the specification: confirmed together with Q9.15 (revision below).
docs/decisions.md:312:- **P23** Precedence between decisions, rows and drafts — Recorded decisions govern. An accepted row supersedes a recorded rule only through an explicitly identified, owner-approved revision (Q5.1/Q5.4 for OD45/OD87, Q6.4 for TYPE-22, Q2.8 for TRAIT-1, Q9.15/P3 for generated chapters). R4's replacements govern conflicting draft recommendations. Before your acceptance is recorded, every passage R4 F18 lists is reconciled (capability inference, generated chapters, roadmap authority, assurance wording, restart order and retention, Phase E, freeze dependencies, superseded Core recommendations), and historical conflicting text is marked superseded.
